# The 3200 px captures are INTERMEDIATES. The pages serve the derived WebP, and
# `node tools/screenshots.mjs` remakes both from the application in one command,
# so committing 12 MB of PNG to derive 4.5 MB of WebP from puts the same picture
# in the repository twice and makes every regeneration a large diff.
#
# The exceptions are every PNG the SITE ITSELF SERVES. That is the criterion,
# and getting it wrong shipped a live defect: the rule below started with two
# exceptions, then four more PNGs were generated — the favicons, the touch icon
# and the documentation card — and the rule swallowed all four. They existed on
# disk, the pages referenced them, and they were 404 on the deployed site.
#
# GitHub Pages serves the REPOSITORY, and there is no Pages build workflow, so
# anything the HTML names has to be committed. `node tools/check-assets.mjs`
# enforces exactly that and runs in CI; if you add a PNG the pages reference,
# add its negation here or that check will fail.
#
# (The earlier comment said the exceptions were "files nothing derives". That
# was never true: tools/webp.mjs derives og-card.png.)
*.png
!SnmpLens.png
!og-card.png
!og-card-docs.png
!favicon-48.png
!favicon-192.png
!apple-touch-icon.png
